1
00:00:00,510 --> 00:00:01,940
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,940 --> 00:00:03,480
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:07,780 --> 00:00:08,950
(Episode 36)

4
00:00:09,050 --> 00:00:10,450
Hello, Dr. Ju.

5
00:00:12,450 --> 00:00:13,720
Ma'am.

6
00:00:15,290 --> 00:00:17,460
There was something urgent
I had to tell you, so I came over.

7
00:00:25,360 --> 00:00:27,330
Are you feeling unwell?

8
00:00:28,170 --> 00:00:29,300
Please, have a seat first.

9
00:00:38,910 --> 00:00:39,910
Ma'am?

10
00:00:46,850 --> 00:00:49,520
I guess I am getting fired.
What a mess.

11
00:00:55,030 --> 00:00:56,960
I want to go see that play
with you, Dr. Ju.

12
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:00,830
- Excuse me?
- Come to think of it,

13
00:01:00,930 --> 00:01:01,970
there is no reason I cannot go.

14
00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:04,740
I really want to see that play.

15
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:06,570
Let us go together, Dr. Ju.

16
00:01:07,840 --> 00:01:10,680
Sure. That is a great decision.

17
00:01:11,180 --> 00:01:12,210
Let us go together.

18
00:01:13,880 --> 00:01:14,880
Okay.

19
00:01:24,390 --> 00:01:25,860
I am back.

20
00:01:31,660 --> 00:01:33,630
Did you need me to do anything?

21
00:01:35,070 --> 00:01:37,500
No, just this here
in front of you. This.

22
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:41,340
This right here?

23
00:01:42,110 --> 00:01:43,780
I think we need to clear
this out quickly,

24
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:45,840
so please take it away.

25
00:01:47,410 --> 00:01:50,520
- Pardon?
- What? Are you curious?

26
00:01:50,650 --> 00:01:52,480
You can open it if you are curious.

27
00:01:57,560 --> 00:02:00,430
Rice cakes?
What are these rice cakes for?

28
00:02:01,360 --> 00:02:04,000
Those rice cakes are very sweet,

29
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:07,000
and more than anything,
they are total calorie bombs.

30
00:02:07,970 --> 00:02:10,700
So when your brain is not working,
they work like a charm.

31
00:02:11,870 --> 00:02:13,970
I thought your brain
needed to be sharp...

32
00:02:14,040 --> 00:02:17,240
for you to focus properly
on the assignment I gave you,

33
00:02:17,310 --> 00:02:19,740
so I got them for you.

34
00:02:20,380 --> 00:02:21,650
Judging by your expression,

35
00:02:21,710 --> 00:02:22,710
the assignment I gave you...

36
00:02:22,780 --> 00:02:24,850
has you worried sick...

37
00:02:24,920 --> 00:02:27,150
and feeling gloomy. Have some.

38
00:02:30,020 --> 00:02:31,220
Thank you. I'll enjoy them.

39
00:02:33,260 --> 00:02:37,760
But I am not feeling down
because of your assignment at all.

40
00:02:39,030 --> 00:02:40,030
Really?

41
00:02:40,730 --> 00:02:43,540
- Then what?
- My mom said she came by briefly,

42
00:02:43,700 --> 00:02:44,840
so I just came back from seeing her.

43
00:02:47,040 --> 00:02:48,210
I just feel a bit...

44
00:02:49,270 --> 00:02:52,710
- Did something bad happen at home?
- Well...

45
00:02:53,710 --> 00:02:56,410
I moved out on my own.

46
00:02:57,320 --> 00:02:59,150
But Mom asked me to move back in,

47
00:02:59,280 --> 00:03:00,990
and I just told her no
and came back up.

48
00:03:02,150 --> 00:03:03,720
I think she was really hurt.

49
00:03:06,160 --> 00:03:08,190
Actually, I was adopted
when I was five.

50
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:14,800
Is that so?

51
00:03:15,570 --> 00:03:18,340
When I was young,
my parents passed away,

52
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:19,600
so Grandma raised me.

53
00:03:20,670 --> 00:03:21,910
That is why I lived
in the same house...

54
00:03:21,970 --> 00:03:23,010
with my uncle's family.

55
00:03:26,480 --> 00:03:27,580
Why are you looking at me like that?

56
00:03:28,010 --> 00:03:30,650
Well, you...

57
00:03:31,120 --> 00:03:33,480
Sharing personal stories
so comfortably...

58
00:03:34,390 --> 00:03:35,620
It just surprised me a bit.

59
00:03:37,690 --> 00:03:39,190
I usually do not, but...

60
00:03:42,630 --> 00:03:44,900
When I decide
the moment calls for it,

61
00:03:45,160 --> 00:03:47,570
I just speak up. That is all.

62
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:49,800
And Kang Da Mi.

63
00:03:50,840 --> 00:03:52,240
Yes, go ahead.

64
00:03:55,440 --> 00:03:59,280
This is the workplace, isn't it?
Now, back to work...

65
00:03:59,710 --> 00:04:01,810
Just like this
sticky rice cake here,

66
00:04:01,980 --> 00:04:06,480
if you really want to succeed
as a designer,

67
00:04:06,950 --> 00:04:08,720
sticking close by my office...

68
00:04:08,790 --> 00:04:11,290
and observing and learning
as much as possible would be wise.

69
00:04:13,090 --> 00:04:14,090
Pardon?

70
00:04:14,460 --> 00:04:16,760
In short, do not wander off
pointlessly...

71
00:04:16,830 --> 00:04:19,360
and advertise how gloomy you are
to everyone around you.

72
00:04:19,730 --> 00:04:20,930
If other people see that,

73
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:22,770
they will think I am mistreating
you, will they not?

74
00:04:23,530 --> 00:04:24,540
Look how nice I am to you.

75
00:04:25,340 --> 00:04:26,800
I even bought you sticky rice cake.

76
00:04:28,040 --> 00:04:29,940
I am sorry. I will be more careful.

77
00:04:49,230 --> 00:04:50,360
Oh, my back.

78
00:04:53,870 --> 00:04:55,370
Brother-in-law? No, wait.

79
00:04:56,500 --> 00:04:57,570
Kang Hak Sung?

80
00:04:58,640 --> 00:05:02,010
What on earth?
How dare he show his face here?

81
00:05:03,110 --> 00:05:05,340
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

82
00:05:07,980 --> 00:05:10,620
I doubted my eyes,
but it really is you.

83
00:05:11,320 --> 00:05:12,580
Brother-in-law? No.

84
00:05:13,620 --> 00:05:16,090
How dare you show your face here?

85
00:05:17,360 --> 00:05:20,660
- Sister-in-law.
- Who are you calling sister-in-law?

86
00:05:21,260 --> 00:05:24,900
Even fleas have some decency.
You two as a couple...

87
00:05:25,060 --> 00:05:26,500
have completely tossed
your consciences away.

88
00:05:26,760 --> 00:05:28,500
Are you determined to put
my sister in the hospital?

89
00:05:28,570 --> 00:05:29,900
Why did you come here?

90
00:05:30,070 --> 00:05:32,940
That is not what matters right now.

91
00:05:33,240 --> 00:05:36,440
Someone is going to end up dead
in there.

92
00:05:36,640 --> 00:05:38,510
Please go inside
and stop them. Please?

93
00:05:39,210 --> 00:05:40,450
What on earth are you talking about?

94
00:05:44,880 --> 00:05:45,980
Mi Mi, wait.

95
00:05:46,080 --> 00:05:47,790
(Consultation Room)

96
00:05:47,890 --> 00:05:52,160
What did you say to Dr. Ju?
Did you really tell him everything?

97
00:05:52,960 --> 00:05:55,390
Why? Are you getting nervous?

98
00:05:56,690 --> 00:05:57,700
Get out of my way.

99
00:06:04,440 --> 00:06:05,740
What do I do?

100
00:06:10,910 --> 00:06:11,910
So...

101
00:06:12,910 --> 00:06:14,580
Are there more appointments
scheduled for today?

102
00:06:15,750 --> 00:06:18,750
Yes, another is due in ten minutes.

103
00:06:19,280 --> 00:06:21,620
Well, there is, but...

104
00:06:22,020 --> 00:06:24,260
Show them inside
as soon as they arrive.

105
00:06:25,590 --> 00:06:26,860
Yes, of course, Dr. Ju.

106
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:32,760
She must not have said
anything major.

107
00:06:34,800 --> 00:06:35,800
Wait.

108
00:06:36,630 --> 00:06:38,970
Then what in the world did those two
talk about in there?

109
00:06:40,540 --> 00:06:42,340
Are you okay, Mi Mi?

110
00:06:42,940 --> 00:06:44,310
Why did you go in there?

111
00:06:44,410 --> 00:06:45,710
(Ju Kyung Ho Internal Medicine)

112
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:47,280
Hey, Kang Hak Sung.

113
00:06:48,010 --> 00:06:49,010
What?

114
00:06:49,510 --> 00:06:50,520
Yes?

115
00:06:50,880 --> 00:06:54,190
I am only going to say this once,
so listen carefully.

116
00:06:55,620 --> 00:06:57,860
Sure, go ahead.

117
00:06:59,360 --> 00:07:00,630
This building is mine.

118
00:07:01,430 --> 00:07:02,830
This restaurant is mine.

119
00:07:03,960 --> 00:07:06,100
Which means this alley
is my territory.

120
00:07:07,600 --> 00:07:09,500
Never set foot around here again.

121
00:07:10,030 --> 00:07:11,040
Do you understand?

122
00:07:12,440 --> 00:07:13,540
Yes, I will do that.

123
00:07:14,770 --> 00:07:15,770
I am sorry.

124
00:07:17,580 --> 00:07:20,810
(Ju Kyung Ho Internal Medicine,
Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

125
00:07:23,210 --> 00:07:24,250
You heard her, right?

126
00:07:24,880 --> 00:07:26,150
Consider yourself lucky...

127
00:07:26,220 --> 00:07:27,950
that my sister is too polite
to push it further.

128
00:07:41,170 --> 00:07:42,170
Mi Mi.

129
00:07:42,400 --> 00:07:45,400
You spilled everything
to Dr. Ju, right?

130
00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:48,940
You told him to fire that sly fox,
did you not?

131
00:07:51,380 --> 00:07:52,480
As long as those two
stay out of my sight,

132
00:07:52,510 --> 00:07:53,740
that is enough.

133
00:07:54,880 --> 00:07:57,050
Do not go gossiping
to Dr. Ju either.

134
00:07:57,110 --> 00:07:59,150
What, is your heart
as wide as the ocean?

135
00:07:59,350 --> 00:08:01,020
Why are you letting them
off the hook?

136
00:08:01,220 --> 00:08:02,850
Why would you keep quiet?

137
00:08:03,050 --> 00:08:05,660
It is just spitting in my own face.
I do not even want to speak of it.

138
00:08:06,260 --> 00:08:07,260
Can you not understand that?

139
00:08:07,490 --> 00:08:10,030
Then why did you go to the clinic
in the first place?

140
00:08:11,230 --> 00:08:12,600
Kang Hak Sung said...

141
00:08:12,660 --> 00:08:14,570
you looked like you were going
to kill someone...

142
00:08:14,630 --> 00:08:15,930
and begged me to stop you.

143
00:08:17,170 --> 00:08:18,800
I went to ask why
I am not getting better...

144
00:08:18,870 --> 00:08:20,240
even though I have been
taking my medicine.

145
00:08:21,510 --> 00:08:23,940
Go check on the broth
so it does not boil down too much.

146
00:08:24,340 --> 00:08:26,380
I need to go inside
and cool my head.

147
00:08:26,980 --> 00:08:29,110
Okay. Got it.

148
00:08:30,310 --> 00:08:31,680
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

149
00:08:33,850 --> 00:08:35,790
Is she cursed this year
or something?

150
00:08:36,990 --> 00:08:40,860
How can not a single day go by
without some kind of drama?

151
00:08:42,290 --> 00:08:44,000
Oh, the broth will boil down.

152
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:48,970
She seems terribly upset.

153
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:52,970
What if she stubbornly refuses
to drink this too?

154
00:09:02,510 --> 00:09:03,510
Mi Mi.

155
00:09:04,020 --> 00:09:05,620
Even just out of respect for
your mother-in-law's devotion,

156
00:09:05,680 --> 00:09:09,050
could you drink this, please?

157
00:09:10,520 --> 00:09:12,160
Why should I drink this?

158
00:09:12,690 --> 00:09:14,390
Go give it to your son instead.

159
00:09:16,190 --> 00:09:17,190
Mi Mi.

160
00:09:20,130 --> 00:09:21,830
After what I've done to her...

161
00:09:22,430 --> 00:09:24,940
I deserve whatever she throws at me.

162
00:09:26,400 --> 00:09:28,310
I just hope
she does not throw it away.

163
00:09:30,610 --> 00:09:33,740
Mother, were you here?
What are you doing?

164
00:09:34,180 --> 00:09:36,810
You are just in time.

165
00:09:36,880 --> 00:09:39,480
I was just about to head out.

166
00:09:40,280 --> 00:09:42,490
This is for you.

167
00:09:43,090 --> 00:09:45,360
I had it brewed
just for you to take.

168
00:09:45,590 --> 00:09:47,220
Drink it before it gets cold, dear.

169
00:09:48,590 --> 00:09:50,060
Did you get herbal medicine brewed?

170
00:09:50,360 --> 00:09:53,400
- For me to drink?
- That is right.

171
00:09:53,530 --> 00:09:55,900
You have been looking
so pale lately,

172
00:09:56,100 --> 00:09:57,740
so I made a special trip
to get it for you.

173
00:09:58,140 --> 00:09:59,400
Once you finish all of this,

174
00:10:00,100 --> 00:10:03,110
I will even order you
some black goat extract.

175
00:10:04,410 --> 00:10:06,610
You are the one who should be
taking herbal medicine.

176
00:10:07,280 --> 00:10:08,510
I am fine.

177
00:10:08,950 --> 00:10:11,350
Since you already got it,
you should drink it, Mother.

178
00:10:13,280 --> 00:10:14,590
Don't you appreciate the effort...

179
00:10:14,650 --> 00:10:16,350
I made despite my aching legs?

180
00:10:17,720 --> 00:10:20,560
I will take it. Thank you.

181
00:10:21,530 --> 00:10:22,830
The thing is, Mother,

182
00:10:23,330 --> 00:10:25,530
my stomach feels a bit upset
right now,

183
00:10:25,630 --> 00:10:27,300
so I will warm it up
and drink it later.

184
00:10:30,070 --> 00:10:31,940
You say you'll drink it later...

185
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:33,770
only to dump it
down the sink, right?

186
00:10:34,610 --> 00:10:38,440
Why would I do that?
How could I possibly...

187
00:10:40,040 --> 00:10:41,450
Give it to me. I'll drink it.

188
00:10:42,450 --> 00:10:43,610
There you go.

189
00:10:44,280 --> 00:10:45,280
Good girl.

190
00:10:51,720 --> 00:10:54,160
What is the matter?
Why are you spitting it out?

191
00:11:01,530 --> 00:11:03,800
What on earth is going on?

192
00:11:08,770 --> 00:11:11,880
Why are you throwing it up?
What a waste.

193
00:11:18,520 --> 00:11:20,420
- Is it done?
- Yes, CEO Jeon.

194
00:11:24,060 --> 00:11:29,960
(Hwanggeum Apparel)

195
00:11:30,130 --> 00:11:31,860
It is an honor
for Summit Two Partners to join...

196
00:11:31,930 --> 00:11:34,670
Hwanggeum Apparel's
brilliant growth, CEO Jeon.

197
00:11:36,870 --> 00:11:40,540
I am very delighted as well.
Let us move forward together.

198
00:11:41,510 --> 00:11:42,840
You will not regret this.

199
00:11:52,080 --> 00:11:54,190
- You wanted to see me?
- Please, come in.

200
00:11:54,420 --> 00:11:55,720
I called you up for a moment...

201
00:11:55,850 --> 00:11:57,190
because I particularly
wanted to introduce you.

202
00:11:57,890 --> 00:12:00,590
This is Jaden Cha,
who has joined our company...

203
00:12:00,860 --> 00:12:01,930
as our head designer.

204
00:12:03,230 --> 00:12:04,500
I knew you were a designer...

205
00:12:04,600 --> 00:12:05,900
who became a success story
in New York,

206
00:12:06,100 --> 00:12:07,160
and now I get to meet you in person.

207
00:12:08,430 --> 00:12:09,430
I have high expectations.

208
00:12:10,800 --> 00:12:13,540
Hello. It is a pleasure to meet you.
I am Cha Seung Yun,

209
00:12:13,640 --> 00:12:15,670
the head designer, Jaden Cha.
Nice to meet you.

210
00:12:16,970 --> 00:12:19,310
CEO Jeon, you can now head
to the reserved restaurant.

211
00:12:20,580 --> 00:12:23,250
We should make a toast now
that the contract is sealed, right?

212
00:12:23,380 --> 00:12:25,520
Because it is a happy day...

213
00:12:25,580 --> 00:12:27,280
for both Summit Two Partners
and Hwanggeum Apparel.

214
00:12:27,890 --> 00:12:28,890
Sounds wonderful.

215
00:12:32,720 --> 00:12:34,730
Who really owns
that seven percent stake,

216
00:12:34,830 --> 00:12:36,060
Aunt Jin Hee?

217
00:12:37,060 --> 00:12:39,930
I still hope my suspicions
do not turn into certainty.

218
00:12:40,560 --> 00:12:43,200
Hold on tight until then.

219
00:12:46,700 --> 00:12:47,940
Jaden Cha, won't you join us?

220
00:12:48,240 --> 00:12:50,340
Thank you so much for the offer,

221
00:12:50,410 --> 00:12:52,780
but I have another engagement
afterward, so next time.

222
00:12:54,280 --> 00:12:55,280
Shall we?

223
00:13:03,050 --> 00:13:05,890
So you are saying
your feelings are hurt?

224
00:13:07,990 --> 00:13:08,990
Yes, Mother.

225
00:13:11,060 --> 00:13:12,330
I know you...

226
00:13:12,930 --> 00:13:15,570
I know you have never been fond
of her,

227
00:13:16,470 --> 00:13:17,800
but still...

228
00:13:18,040 --> 00:13:19,840
I never imagined...

229
00:13:19,900 --> 00:13:21,510
you would go as far as to have
a background check run on her.

230
00:13:23,640 --> 00:13:25,240
Ever since she married
into our family,

231
00:13:25,310 --> 00:13:26,740
she raised Do Yun so well
all these years...

232
00:13:27,180 --> 00:13:28,710
and helped grow the company too.

233
00:13:28,810 --> 00:13:30,810
Even you must acknowledge
that, Mother.

234
00:13:31,650 --> 00:13:33,520
I do acknowledge that.

235
00:13:33,850 --> 00:13:35,520
Even a birth mother couldn't...

236
00:13:35,590 --> 00:13:37,860
have raised him with more devotion.

237
00:13:39,760 --> 00:13:41,930
You have no idea
how terrible I felt for her.

238
00:13:43,960 --> 00:13:45,130
Besides, Mother,

239
00:13:45,900 --> 00:13:48,030
these days, changing one's name...

240
00:13:48,600 --> 00:13:50,700
is common practice
for all kinds of reasons.

241
00:13:51,040 --> 00:13:52,200
From what she told me,

242
00:13:52,540 --> 00:13:54,810
she grew up so lonely
and struggled so much,

243
00:13:55,010 --> 00:13:57,170
so she changed her name
when she met me...

244
00:13:57,640 --> 00:14:00,080
to one fit for our Hwanggeum family.

245
00:14:00,340 --> 00:14:03,510
So she changed it
because she wanted a fresh start.

246
00:14:04,050 --> 00:14:06,150
Fine. Well, it is not that...

247
00:14:06,220 --> 00:14:10,050
- I do not understand how she felt.
- You understand, right?

248
00:14:11,020 --> 00:14:13,920
Then please trust my wife
from now on...

249
00:14:14,260 --> 00:14:16,860
and treat her accordingly, Mother.

250
00:14:17,860 --> 00:14:20,600
Even if she did not show it,
she must have been deeply hurt.

251
00:14:20,930 --> 00:14:22,730
How could she not be?

252
00:14:23,570 --> 00:14:25,870
She is truly soft-hearted inside.

253
00:14:28,110 --> 00:14:29,510
Are you done talking?

254
00:14:31,180 --> 00:14:32,180
Yes.

255
00:14:32,640 --> 00:14:35,650
Is that so?
If you are done, then leave.

256
00:14:36,410 --> 00:14:38,880
I am tired, so I need to lie down.

257
00:14:39,880 --> 00:14:41,050
You will drop...

258
00:14:41,790 --> 00:14:43,120
the background check, right?

259
00:14:44,590 --> 00:14:48,190
If you are this upset about it,
what choice do I have?

260
00:14:49,560 --> 00:14:51,060
I do not want to lose favor...

261
00:14:51,400 --> 00:14:53,430
with my only remaining child.

262
00:14:56,200 --> 00:14:57,530
Thank you, Mother.

263
00:14:59,100 --> 00:15:00,540
Get some rest, then.

264
00:15:10,410 --> 00:15:12,220
Soft-hearted?

265
00:15:17,320 --> 00:15:20,620
He still only believes what he sees.

266
00:15:29,170 --> 00:15:32,240
CEO Jeon.
Congratulations on closing the deal.

267
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:34,440
Well, it was the natural outcome.

268
00:15:35,140 --> 00:15:37,440
We shouldn't keep them waiting,
so let us head down too.

269
00:15:38,440 --> 00:15:39,940
(CEO Jeon Jin Hee)

270
00:15:44,650 --> 00:15:47,580
- What is the matter, CEO Jeon?
- About Manager Kang.

271
00:15:49,450 --> 00:15:50,850
What are you going to do
with Kang Da Mi?

272
00:15:51,320 --> 00:15:52,320
Pardon?

273
00:15:53,990 --> 00:15:56,430
Something about her
just rubs me the wrong way.

274
00:15:57,260 --> 00:16:00,600
I really do not want
someone like that around my son.

275
00:16:02,500 --> 00:16:03,930
What do you think,
Assistant Manager Kang?

276
00:16:04,940 --> 00:16:07,370
Since you asked, I will be honest.

277
00:16:08,140 --> 00:16:10,470
She drops by Product Planning
quite often,

278
00:16:11,010 --> 00:16:12,910
and Team Leader Cha
is helping her out...

279
00:16:12,980 --> 00:16:14,450
and looking after her
a bit too much.

280
00:16:14,610 --> 00:16:15,610
Really?

281
00:16:16,750 --> 00:16:17,820
Now what?

282
00:16:21,190 --> 00:16:23,220
As the CEO, I shouldn't have
to concern myself...

283
00:16:23,350 --> 00:16:25,460
with someone like her, should I?

284
00:16:26,090 --> 00:16:27,220
In that case...

285
00:16:28,290 --> 00:16:30,130
You're on my side,
Assistant Manager Kang.

286
00:16:31,230 --> 00:16:33,030
I'd appreciate it
if you handled this...

287
00:16:33,100 --> 00:16:35,000
smoothly on your own.

288
00:16:35,900 --> 00:16:38,140
Yes. Yes, CEO Jeon.

289
00:16:43,970 --> 00:16:46,010
She means I should make her
quit on her own, right?

290
00:16:55,620 --> 00:16:57,420
The design is pretty,

291
00:16:58,120 --> 00:16:59,960
and the price is reasonable,

292
00:17:01,630 --> 00:17:06,060
so why didn't people buy it?
I really can't figure out why.

293
00:17:07,970 --> 00:17:09,030
I have no idea.

294
00:17:14,040 --> 00:17:16,140
Why?

295
00:17:16,210 --> 00:17:18,380
Why were you not
popular with people?

296
00:17:20,480 --> 00:17:21,510
What was it?

297
00:17:24,080 --> 00:17:25,080
Are you busy?

298
00:17:25,720 --> 00:17:27,520
Welcome, Team Leader Cha.

299
00:17:27,850 --> 00:17:29,150
Where's Head Designer Cha?

300
00:17:29,450 --> 00:17:31,220
He said there was a lot of work,
so I came down first.

301
00:17:32,420 --> 00:17:34,430
He stepped downstairs
to the design room...

302
00:17:34,490 --> 00:17:36,190
for a brief meeting.

303
00:17:36,530 --> 00:17:40,030
Since they're remaking
the spring summer line,

304
00:17:40,130 --> 00:17:41,300
everyone is on high alert.

305
00:17:42,130 --> 00:17:43,230
You haven't eaten either, right?

306
00:17:45,670 --> 00:17:46,800
Have some of this while you work.

307
00:17:49,070 --> 00:17:50,270
It's sushi.

308
00:17:50,670 --> 00:17:53,010
You really didn't need
to do this for me.

309
00:17:53,310 --> 00:17:55,380
We all work to eat, don't we?

310
00:18:01,520 --> 00:18:03,520
My timing was just right.

311
00:18:05,260 --> 00:18:06,320
Thank you.

312
00:18:07,220 --> 00:18:09,730
Well, they do say even ghosts
look better on a full stomach.

313
00:18:09,790 --> 00:18:11,830
My grandma always said that.

314
00:18:12,560 --> 00:18:14,300
I'll eat quickly
and get back to work.

315
00:18:15,900 --> 00:18:18,470
Sounds like your assignment...

316
00:18:18,540 --> 00:18:21,140
is really giving you a hard time.

317
00:18:21,770 --> 00:18:22,870
By the way, Da Mi,

318
00:18:22,940 --> 00:18:24,580
do you live with
your grandmother too?

319
00:18:25,780 --> 00:18:26,780
Yes.

320
00:18:27,310 --> 00:18:28,350
Oh, right.

321
00:18:28,480 --> 00:18:30,810
You were raised by your grandmother
too, weren't you?

322
00:18:30,880 --> 00:18:32,680
Yes, how did you know that?

323
00:18:33,850 --> 00:18:35,520
Did Se Na tell you?

324
00:18:36,050 --> 00:18:38,260
Head Designer Cha told me.

325
00:18:38,990 --> 00:18:41,290
Seeing how well
all three of you turned out,

326
00:18:41,360 --> 00:18:44,800
your aunt and uncle
must be wonderful people.

327
00:18:45,560 --> 00:18:46,560
Pardon?

328
00:18:48,130 --> 00:18:51,000
My sister, who you met
at the department store,

329
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:52,070
and I have the same parents.

330
00:18:53,100 --> 00:18:54,170
As for Seung Yun...

331
00:18:56,070 --> 00:18:58,410
Then the head designer is?

332
00:19:00,380 --> 00:19:03,850
His parents passed away. So...

333
00:19:04,620 --> 00:19:05,650
he's my cousin.

334
00:19:06,980 --> 00:19:08,490
He's our family's eldest grandson.

335
00:19:11,360 --> 00:19:12,720
Still, we grew up together...

336
00:19:12,890 --> 00:19:13,960
in the same house
with our grandmother.

337
00:19:14,060 --> 00:19:15,460
We're practically real brothers.

338
00:19:16,890 --> 00:19:18,130
Though, this is surprising.

339
00:19:19,460 --> 00:19:20,760
What is?

340
00:19:21,800 --> 00:19:24,230
Ever since he was young,

341
00:19:24,540 --> 00:19:27,100
Seung Yun has never been the type
to easily open up about himself.

342
00:19:29,710 --> 00:19:30,710
I see.

343
00:19:44,450 --> 00:19:46,620
Why does my stomach feel so bloated?

344
00:19:47,560 --> 00:19:49,960
I haven't even eaten anything,
but I keep gagging.

345
00:19:55,200 --> 00:19:57,200
You're a real mess, Jo Mi Mi.

346
00:20:01,840 --> 00:20:02,840
(Logistics: Packaging Supply Sorting
and Production Support)

347
00:20:02,910 --> 00:20:03,970
(Fruit Shop: Orders and Purchasing,
Construction: Material Intake, Sort)

348
00:20:04,840 --> 00:20:06,710
Wait, are you telling me...

349
00:20:06,780 --> 00:20:09,180
to load and unload boxes
at a distribution center?

350
00:20:09,680 --> 00:20:11,080
Fruit delivery?

351
00:20:11,820 --> 00:20:12,880
And what is this?

352
00:20:13,980 --> 00:20:17,090
Luckily, you do have
a driver's license, dear client.

353
00:20:17,320 --> 00:20:20,790
You do know you're in no position
to be picky about jobs, right?

354
00:20:23,330 --> 00:20:24,330
I suppose...

355
00:20:24,390 --> 00:20:26,430
Who am I to be picky
at a time like this?

356
00:20:26,830 --> 00:20:27,830
Great.

357
00:20:27,970 --> 00:20:30,600
Then put all your energy
into getting any job you can.

358
00:20:33,040 --> 00:20:35,170
By the way,
why do you look so gaunt?

359
00:20:36,270 --> 00:20:38,380
Right, I bought something for you.

360
00:20:39,040 --> 00:20:41,350
What is it? I'm not hungry.

361
00:20:42,280 --> 00:20:46,450
From now on,
you must never skip a meal.

362
00:20:46,650 --> 00:20:48,650
You have to eat well and sleep well
no matter what.

363
00:20:48,750 --> 00:20:50,390
That way, you can make
at least some money right away.

364
00:20:50,450 --> 00:20:51,520
You have to earn money to pay my...

365
00:20:52,560 --> 00:20:56,060
I mean,
to pay back our company's money.

366
00:21:09,840 --> 00:21:11,340
That scumbag, Kim Pro,

367
00:21:11,410 --> 00:21:12,640
who ran off with nearly
a million dollars,

368
00:21:13,680 --> 00:21:16,450
is probably stuffing his face
somewhere right now, right?

369
00:21:17,250 --> 00:21:19,850
Let us eat. Fine, I will eat.

370
00:21:24,590 --> 00:21:26,420
Even if you do not have
an appetite right now,

371
00:21:26,520 --> 00:21:27,890
channel that anger...

372
00:21:27,960 --> 00:21:29,660
into a determination
to get back on your feet.

373
00:21:30,090 --> 00:21:31,500
Show it through your actions,
Dae Chi.

374
00:21:33,460 --> 00:21:35,030
"Dae Chi"?

375
00:21:35,370 --> 00:21:37,300
Oh, sorry...

376
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:41,270
I have two older brothers at home,
so it just slipped out.

377
00:21:41,570 --> 00:21:43,710
Hurry and finish up.
Chew thoroughly.

378
00:21:45,610 --> 00:21:46,710
Shouldn't you get going, though?

379
00:21:47,810 --> 00:21:50,350
I doubt I am the only debtor
you are assigned to.

380
00:21:51,010 --> 00:21:52,980
You might choke.

381
00:21:54,320 --> 00:21:56,690
Here, drink some cola.

382
00:22:00,660 --> 00:22:04,800
- Drink slowly.
- Must be nice to be young.

383
00:22:08,200 --> 00:22:09,200
Wait a second.

384
00:22:09,870 --> 00:22:12,040
- What is it, Dad?
- Hold on, Su Ah.

385
00:22:12,640 --> 00:22:14,940
Isn't that my own flesh
and blood over there?

386
00:22:15,510 --> 00:22:18,510
It is my uncle. Uncle.

387
00:22:19,710 --> 00:22:22,250
He claimed he was working from home,

388
00:22:22,310 --> 00:22:23,610
and here he is
flirting with a woman.

389
00:22:23,680 --> 00:22:26,280
He still has a long way to go
to get his act together.

390
00:22:26,520 --> 00:22:28,850
Kang Dae Chi,
you are so busted, you punk.

391
00:22:29,350 --> 00:22:32,860
Dad, who is that woman next to him?
She is really pretty.

392
00:22:34,790 --> 00:22:38,760
No, your mom was prettier.
Sweetheart, let us head inside.

393
00:22:46,100 --> 00:22:47,500
The great Kang Dae Chi...

394
00:22:50,010 --> 00:22:51,880
How did I wind up taking a burger...

395
00:22:51,940 --> 00:22:54,040
as charity from a woman under 30?

396
00:23:05,290 --> 00:23:06,290
You startled me.

397
00:23:07,560 --> 00:23:10,030
For someone working from home,
you sure are busy.

398
00:23:11,760 --> 00:23:14,100
I just stepped out
for some fresh air.

399
00:23:14,660 --> 00:23:17,330
I was suffocating, being cooped up
working at home.

400
00:23:18,600 --> 00:23:21,840
So suffocating that you went
on a date with a woman,

401
00:23:22,310 --> 00:23:24,940
enjoying a delicious burger?

402
00:23:26,040 --> 00:23:27,040
Man,

403
00:23:27,510 --> 00:23:29,280
she was even feeding you cola
with her own hands.

404
00:23:30,080 --> 00:23:31,280
You saw that?

405
00:23:31,520 --> 00:23:33,650
Would I be calling you out
if I hadn't?

406
00:23:34,220 --> 00:23:36,020
Are you really in a position...

407
00:23:36,190 --> 00:23:38,290
to be running around
meeting women right now?

408
00:23:38,920 --> 00:23:40,620
She looked way younger than you.

409
00:23:40,890 --> 00:23:43,360
She might look young,
but she is plenty old enough.

410
00:23:44,260 --> 00:23:46,200
- And, Gang Nam...
- And what?

411
00:23:47,760 --> 00:23:49,700
I will tell you everything if you
promise to keep your mouth shut.

412
00:23:49,870 --> 00:23:52,670
Hey, I am your brother.

413
00:23:53,640 --> 00:23:55,610
Why? Is it serious?

414
00:23:56,370 --> 00:23:59,240
Does she know that you are
1.13 million dollars in debt?

415
00:23:59,610 --> 00:24:00,880
She is not my girlfriend.

416
00:24:03,350 --> 00:24:04,410
She is my creditor.

417
00:24:05,250 --> 00:24:07,050
She works for a loan company
on debt collection.

418
00:24:08,890 --> 00:24:10,450
What kind of debt collector
feeds cola to their debtor?

419
00:24:10,620 --> 00:24:11,620
Coming to collect debt...

420
00:24:11,690 --> 00:24:15,130
- and feeding the debtor cola?
- I owe that loan company...

421
00:24:15,260 --> 00:24:16,260
around 200,000 dollars,

422
00:24:16,730 --> 00:24:19,130
and she is keeping an eye on me
in case I do something reckless.

423
00:24:19,760 --> 00:24:21,060
She felt sorry for me,

424
00:24:21,200 --> 00:24:22,570
so she bought me a burger
and some cola.

425
00:24:23,170 --> 00:24:25,100
Wait, "something reckless"?

426
00:24:27,240 --> 00:24:29,510
Hey, do not tell me you...

427
00:24:30,740 --> 00:24:34,280
I am not going to the Han River.
I am not going to kill myself.

428
00:24:35,080 --> 00:24:36,110
Right.

429
00:24:36,180 --> 00:24:40,250
You had better keep that resolve
safe and sound, Kang Dae Chi.

430
00:24:41,890 --> 00:24:42,920
Let us go in.

431
00:24:44,090 --> 00:24:45,160
Hey, but Dae Chi.

432
00:24:45,890 --> 00:24:47,260
What is the name
of that loan company?

433
00:24:47,690 --> 00:24:48,690
Why do you ask?

434
00:24:48,930 --> 00:24:52,100
Well, their collection
method seems...

435
00:24:52,160 --> 00:24:54,200
pretty different from other places.

436
00:24:54,870 --> 00:24:59,040
If I can use them too,
I want to look into it.

437
00:24:59,940 --> 00:25:01,710
Introduce me to your agent sometime.

438
00:25:01,770 --> 00:25:04,170
That is so embarrassing...

439
00:25:04,880 --> 00:25:06,380
Please talk some sense.

440
00:25:08,510 --> 00:25:10,010
Hey, wait...

441
00:25:10,080 --> 00:25:16,190
- What a heartless jerk.
- There you are.

442
00:25:16,820 --> 00:25:18,260
- Gang Nam.
- What is it?

443
00:25:19,360 --> 00:25:20,890
Come to the restaurant right now.

444
00:25:21,360 --> 00:25:23,030
I just brought Su Ah home,
and I am supposed to wash her...

445
00:25:23,090 --> 00:25:24,660
I told her I would read her a book.

446
00:25:24,730 --> 00:25:28,030
Do that later.
Right now, at the restaurant...

447
00:25:32,170 --> 00:25:33,400
What? Really?

448
00:25:39,740 --> 00:25:42,050
Please take good care of Da Mi.

449
00:25:42,780 --> 00:25:44,150
It must be really
uncomfortable for you...

450
00:25:44,680 --> 00:25:46,020
in that tiny room for now.

451
00:25:47,020 --> 00:25:48,350
Do not worry, Mother.

452
00:25:48,950 --> 00:25:50,320
You do not have to
say anything more.

453
00:25:51,350 --> 00:25:53,490
Thank you for taking this
without hesitation.

454
00:25:54,660 --> 00:25:56,890
Da Mi and I will enjoy eating it.

455
00:25:58,500 --> 00:25:59,730
Are you just leaving?

456
00:26:00,500 --> 00:26:02,930
Su Ah should be back from preschool.
Are you leaving without seeing her?

457
00:26:03,730 --> 00:26:07,940
No, I will just go today.
I think that would be better.

458
00:26:08,770 --> 00:26:10,440
You are worried
she will not let you go, right?

459
00:26:12,110 --> 00:26:13,580
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

460
00:26:13,740 --> 00:26:16,180
- You are here? What brings you by?
- Well...

461
00:26:16,250 --> 00:26:19,380
- I will get going, Mother.
- Wait. That must be heavy for you.

462
00:26:19,780 --> 00:26:20,880
Good timing, Gang Nam.

463
00:26:20,950 --> 00:26:23,620
- Take this.
- Should I?

464
00:26:24,290 --> 00:26:25,290
Give it to me.

465
00:26:26,120 --> 00:26:28,390
- Let go.
- Give it to me.

466
00:26:28,930 --> 00:26:31,560
Why did my mom pack
such a huge bundle?

467
00:26:31,900 --> 00:26:32,930
My arm is about to fall off.

468
00:26:36,330 --> 00:26:37,900
Hold on. Mi Seon,
let us go together.

469
00:26:38,300 --> 00:26:39,540
I need to buy something too.

470
00:26:41,270 --> 00:26:42,310
Okay.

471
00:26:43,340 --> 00:26:44,670
All right, let us go.

472
00:26:46,680 --> 00:26:47,680
Mi Mi.

473
00:26:48,240 --> 00:26:50,410
Where are you going again?

474
00:26:51,450 --> 00:26:53,120
Seriously.

475
00:26:55,990 --> 00:26:57,020
Goodness.

476
00:26:57,920 --> 00:27:00,220
This is what happens
when you have a pathetic son.

477
00:27:01,420 --> 00:27:02,660
I had to use
the bundle as an excuse...

478
00:27:03,360 --> 00:27:04,590
to put them in the same taxi.

479
00:27:06,430 --> 00:27:08,570
I should hurry back
to open the shop.

480
00:27:14,140 --> 00:27:15,140
Oh, right.

481
00:27:15,670 --> 00:27:17,240
I was supposed to go see a play.

482
00:27:30,190 --> 00:27:31,590
It is pretty, right?

483
00:27:32,460 --> 00:27:34,760
Yes, it is, but...

484
00:27:35,890 --> 00:27:36,890
No, it is fine.

485
00:27:37,190 --> 00:27:41,500
You do not have to buy it.
Just try it on, okay?

486
00:27:42,400 --> 00:27:44,000
At my age...

487
00:27:44,830 --> 00:27:45,900
The color is too...

488
00:27:45,970 --> 00:27:48,240
Like I said,
you do not have to buy it.

489
00:27:48,740 --> 00:27:50,670
Trying it on is free.

490
00:27:54,980 --> 00:27:57,250
I am only trying it on, okay?

491
00:28:07,120 --> 00:28:09,060
(Mission: Mompossible)

492
00:28:09,160 --> 00:28:13,060
- Can I not wear a dress like this?
- Isn't that for young women?

493
00:28:13,460 --> 00:28:14,460
Jin Hee,

494
00:28:14,660 --> 00:28:18,200
tell me what you want most
right now.

495
00:28:18,270 --> 00:28:19,970
I will grant you anything.

496
00:28:20,400 --> 00:28:23,410
In my opinion, luxury manager
at the department store...

497
00:28:23,710 --> 00:28:26,210
suits you much better, Kang Da Mi.

498
00:28:27,440 --> 00:28:29,450
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
